.TH "CITADEL" "1" "Sep 2026" "AceTeam" "Citadel CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
citadel-whatsapp-rotate-key - Rotate the WhatsApp bridge admin secret (ADMIN_API_KEY)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcitadel whatsapp rotate-key [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate a fresh admin secret for the bridge control plane, atomically
rewrite its 0600 env file (preserving the tenant keys and every other setting),
recreate the bridge so it picks up the new key, and verify the new key
authenticates against the bridge's admin API.

.PP
Only the ADMIN key is rotated. The per-tenant data-plane keys the AceTeam
platform stores are left untouched, so an already-linked WhatsApp session and
its registered api_key keep working.

.PP
The admin key bytes are never printed; only the old and new key fingerprints
(sha256:...) are shown.

.PP
Privileges: the bridge env file is written 0600 and is usually owned by the
root \fBcitadel work\fR worker. Run rotate-key with the SAME privileges that
started the worker (e.g. sudo) so it can rewrite that file and recreate the
bridge.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Show what would rotate (env file path, current fingerprint) without touching anything.

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for rotate-key


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug output

.PP
\fB--no-auto-update\fP[=false]
	Disable automatic update checks and installs for this run (or set CITADEL_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable colorized output

.PP
\fB--node-dir\fP=""
	Override the node config directory (citadel.yaml + services/), bypassing $HOME/ConfigDir resolution. Also settable via CITADEL_NODE_DIR. Scope: manifest/services resolution only -- does NOT redirect network state, the module lockfile, or nodevault.

.PP
\fB--runtime\fP=""
	Container runtime for module containers: docker or podman (default: auto-detect)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcitadel-whatsapp(1)\fP
